# SFT execution status v0.132: full-size streaming staging and worker settings

2026-09-28. Implemented and locally tested the actual opaque-byte copy primitive
for the full-size VM inputs, plus the full-size import unit settings. **202 tests
passed; no real input acquisition, VM action, mount, systemd dispatch, GPU or
training occurred.** This is a component implementation, not a completed native
full-size parent. Gate 5 is still incomplete. The tiny Linux success in v0.130
and full-size metadata/control preparation in v0.131 are unchanged.

## Implemented

`posttraining_vm_fullsize_staging_v1.py` accepts the hash-pinned v0.1 input
selection as bytes and copies streams into an exclusively created input tree
under an already-open private directory. It requests only exact selected keys,
hashes opaque chunks without parsing trainer/model/tokenizer bytes, checks each
response's declared and actual size, and validates SHA-256 before acceptance.
Nested tokenizer paths and root-level trainer files are preserved exactly.

There is one supplied transport call per object, no application retry or resume.
The component requests at most 1 MiB per read and writes at most each object's
bound size. A one-byte EOF probe per object is separately budgeted: up to
48,843,765,465 response-body bytes for a conforming transport, including the
22-byte probe allowance. Normal success returns the exact 48,843,765,443 content
bytes. This is NOT a total network cap: TLS, headers, transport retry behavior,
socket timeouts and a hard process deadline remain the transport/parent's job.
Acquisition is separate from the frozen coordinator's source-read/write budgets.

Files are exclusive, non-symlink, fsynced and mode 0400 after successful copy;
private directory traversal uses directory descriptors and no-follow opens.
Every response body and file writer is closed before a successful return. The
started marker survives failures and success, rejecting reuse of that attempt.
No cleanup removes partial files or evidence. Failure messages retain fixed
codes only. Public `stage_inputs` remains closed; this private primitive does
not grant host admission or acquisition authority.

Mode 0400 is **not filesystem immutability**: the owning user could chmod a
writable backing file. The component explicitly returns read-only mount and
acquisition-cgroup-reaped claims as false. The independently admitted root
parent must terminate/reap acquisition, remove credentials and writable aliases,
and supply verified read-only bind mounts before starting a distinct worker.

`posttraining_vm_fullsize_controls_v1.py` derives settings from the qualified
tiny route: only memory (64 GiB), deadline (3,600 seconds), inaccessible paths
and input/source/output bind paths change. UID/GID 10001, zero swap, tasks 64,
no network, no restart, kill-whole-cgroup, no capabilities, strict system
protection and null logs remain. Inputs and outputs are disk-backed host binds;
the inherited small `/work` tmpfs is scratch, not 48.8-GB input storage. Settings
construction does not mount anything or prove capacity, host identity, resource
enforcement/readback or cumulative native-write limits.

## Verification

- 25 new tests: successful opaque copy, exact paths/modes, stream closure,
  short/overlong/invalid streams, hash/header mismatch, bounded chunks/EOF,
  partial/zero/disk-failed writes, deadlines, fsync/close/transport failure,
  no retry, rejected paths/duplicates/parent conflicts/symlinks, runtime/public
  entry closure, and unchanged inherited controls.
- 177 prior adapter, selection, resource, I/O and coordinator regressions.
- Total: 202 tests, zero failures/errors/skips, 0.408 seconds; Ruff passed.
- The test runtime gate and transport were doubled; only tiny synthetic content
  (including a roughly 1-MiB chunk-boundary case) was copied into temporary files.
  No real 4B tensors, tokenizer data or trainer state was opened.
- Parent audit hook observed zero network and forbidden-payload attempts; no ML
  modules loaded. This hook is not an OS sandbox or native qualification.
- Actual saved control validated against its exact pin: 22 objects,
  48,843,765,443 bytes. Seven v0.131 bindings and four native-success evidence
  bindings verified unchanged. Native result metadata, not model payload, was
  read for that check. No previous evidence/source was edited; no commit/push.

Initial local lint found four long lines, corrected before final verification.
An ad-hoc prior-evidence check first used the wrong metadata dictionary key;
the corrected read-only check validated the four native bindings. Neither was
a remote execution or import attempt.

## Remaining work, without restarting completed qualification

The executable root-parent integration is still missing: authenticated host/
runtime/source closure; the bounded exact-key AWS transport and credential
lifecycle; acquisition cgroup termination/readback; disk-backed layout and
mount/cgroup readback; invoking the existing full-size entry once; independent
package checksum verification, durable retention, and cleanup. The new stream
primitive and settings are reusable pieces of that integration, not its proof.

After that local wiring, bind the total setup/transfer/import/verification/
retention budgets and obtain explicit full-size execution approval. Do not
switch the old generated-only AWS authorization to real data. Do not rerun the
already successful tiny qualification merely to produce another local report.

Current claims: `real_4b_import=false`, `fullsize_host_admission=false`,
`gate_5_complete=false`, `training_authorized=false`, `production_eligible=false`.
Gate 6 GPU smoke/save/resume and SFT remain after real import; no GPU was started.
